## Task ID/Title
Sprint 1 Planning, Meeting Minutes Organization, and GitHub Documentation

## Purpose of AI Use
AI was used to help organize Sprint 1 meeting minutes, brainstorm and clarify team member roles, support sprint planning, and assist with documenting issues, checkpoints, and project details clearly on GitHub.

The AI assistance was mainly used for:
- Sprint planning
- Documentation
- Meeting minute organization
- GitHub issue organization
- Team role clarification
- Checkpoint planning

## Chat Link or Prompt/Response
https://chatgpt.com/s/cx_6ab9a82ab3a08191b4f02a4942ffeebf

https://chatgpt.com/share/6ab9aa72-d7b4-83ea-90a7-11fe43613824

## AI-Suggested Content
The AI suggested ways to:

- Organize Sprint 1 documentation more clearly
- Structure meeting minutes in a professional and consistent format
- Clarify the responsibilities of each team member
- Create measurable Sprint 1 checkpoints
- Organize GitHub issues and project planning
- Structure Sprint 1 documentation according to the project requirements

## Validation
The AI output was validated through manual review and comparison with the official SOEN 341 Sprint 1 project requirements.

The suggestions were also compared with:
- The team's actual decisions
- The current GitHub repository structure
- Work already completed by team members
- Discussions held during team meetings

Some suggestions were adjusted before being used so that they better reflected the team's actual workflow and responsibilities.

## Decision
**Modified before use**

Most of the AI-generated suggestions were useful and were accepted either fully or with minor modifications.

Changes were made when necessary to better match:
- The team's actual responsibilities
- The current state of the GitHub repository
- Sprint 1 requirements
- Decisions made during team meetings

## Reflection
The AI assistance was very helpful and saved a significant amount of time.

It helped organize information that would otherwise have required searching through many different sources and learning several GitHub and Agile-related concepts separately.

The AI was especially useful for turning rough notes and ideas into clearer documentation and more organized project planning.

Through this process, I learned how to better structure:
- Meeting minutes
- Sprint planning documentation
- GitHub issues
- Project checkpoints
- Team responsibilities

The suggestions still required manual review and modification to ensure that they correctly represented the team's work and followed the project requirements.

